Motion denied.description:
Order;
The Court rejects the view of the Defendant that the trial judgment (minus PIP reduction) of $313.72 Dollars is the figure to be viewed in deciding this Motion.  The Jury had no idea of the PIP offset.  The controlling number is the actual amount listed on the jury verdict form.  Based upon that finding, the plaintiff presented facts to successfully demonstrate an entitlement to relief.  Iannachchino v. Ford Motor Co. 451 Mass 623 (2008).  The difference between the verdict and the offer may not be great in terms of actual dollars, however it does represent an almost 2/3 increase.  As such a dismissal of the G.L. c.93A portion of this claim would not be appropriate. The Motion to Dismiss is Denied.  The parties may schedule the matter for further proceedings. (Payne, J)  Parties notified

Applies To: Tanner, Esq., Mark Allan (Attorney) on behalf of Pearson, Susan (Plaintiff); Manitsas, Esq., James M (Attorney) on behalf of Safety Insurance Company (Defendant)

